# Opens a calibration attempt's Data Input tab in the app and checks its observed dataset slot is filled.
#
#   pwsh -NoProfile -WorkingDirectory geodc -File dev/ui.ps1 attach --launch --project dev/sample-projects/sample.gdcproj
#   pwsh -NoProfile -WorkingDirectory geodc -File dev/ui.ps1 do --file dev/ui-scripts/app-open-calibration.ui
#
# The default attempt is in the sample project (`dev/ui.ps1 sample create`). Pick another with
# --var "attempt=<attempt list name>". Works in passive mode. Navigation and selection come from
# lib/app-open-attempt, which also asserts the selected attempt's name. The sample project's attempts already hold
# observed data, so the slot shows Inspect rather than Import (DatasetSlot names both from its SlotId).
@target app
@var attempt=Pitch calibration (INITIAL)

run lib/app-open-attempt page=CalibrationTab attempt='${attempt}' tab=DataInputTab
assert --id DataInputPanel
assert --id AttemptNameInput --exists
assert --id TargetSensorCombo --exists
assert --id InspectObservedButton --exists
